   "evidence": "Lines 265-271 and 279-285 of the new file; `grep \"mellinMoment_|smul|const_mul\" EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/` shows no scaling lemma, and `Parton/PDF/Basic.lean:35` shows `mellinMoment` is a plain integral def with only `mellinMoment_congr`/`mellinMoment_comap` as rewriting API.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Meson/Pdf/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add the generic lemma upstream next to `mellinMoment` (e.g. `mellinMoment_weight_mul : mellinMoment (fun i x Q2 => c i * f i x Q2) n s Q2 = c s * mellinMoment f n s Q2`, plus the matching `Assumptions` transfer for a nonnegative weight), and derive `mellinMoment_valenceModelPdf` and the `momentIntegrable`/`measurable` fields from it; this removes the duplicated `funext ... ring` block and the `rw [PDF.mellinMoment] ... rw [\u2190 PDF.mellinMoment]` round trip.",
   "issue": "The identity `x ^ n * (w * g) = w * (x ^ n * g)` for `valenceModelPdf` is proved twice verbatim \u2014 as a function equality at lines 265-269 (`assumptions_valenceModelPdf.momentIntegrable`) and pointwise at lines 279-282 (`mellinMoment_valenceModelPdf`) \u2014 and nothing in it is meson-specific. Consequently line 283-285 has to unfold and refold the definition (`rw [PDF.mellinMoment, ..., \u2190 PDF.mellinMoment]`) because no scaling lemma exists to rewrite with.",
   "line": 265
  }
